exports[`spine full axis matrix (16 representative cells) > baseline-frontier-balanced: stable spine + body[0] structural fields 1`] = `
{
  "body0": "On one side Lantern Circuit Registry, after standing to rewrite the charter in their own hand; on the other Vantage Ledger Underwriters, holding the last berth they can still afford to hold. And there is the part no one says at the negotiating table: The compact between Lantern Circuit Registry and Vantage Ledger Underwriters fractured after the great rerouting. Salvage from the worst of it is still being sold with the serial numbers filed off. The debt-fleet anchor graveyard presses, Mothallah Corridor-631 III holds, and the one-way capture valve pays for both: the freight surcharge that lands on them no matter who wins. This one is no longer cold, and everyone routing through has repriced accordingly. The dispute has a second floor: Debt-fleet anchor graveyard raised Mothallah Corridor-631 III out of nothing before the gate cooled, on terms the founders never wrote down. Freight insurance for the contested run now costs more than the freight. Neither the one-way capture valve nor Mothallah Corridor-631 III will blink first, and the debt-fleet anchor graveyard absorbs the difference — rationed air while the principals negotiate. Dock crews from the one-way capture valve and Mothallah Corridor-631 III unload under separate armed escorts that pretend not to watch each other.",
  "spineEdgeType": "CONTESTS",
  "spineObjectKind": "namedFaction",
  "spineSubjectKind": "namedFaction",
  "spineSummary": "The compact between Lantern Circuit Registry and Vantage Ledger Underwriters broke after the great rerouting, Everything else in this system is priced against the quarrel between the two of them.",
  "spineVisibility": "contested",
}
`;

exports[`spine full axis matrix (16 representative cells) > baseline-frontier-cinematic: stable spine + body[0] structural fields 1`] = `
{
  "body0": "The fight belongs to Brothers of Choir and Carrion Wake; the bleeding is done at Vow-Breaker Wake. It was always going to come to this, because the arbitration that used to settle this dissolved with its sponsor. The joint maintenance schedule still runs, but each side sends its own inspector to watch the other's. The public channel carries two incompatible traffic advisories for the same lane. Brothers of Choir wants the right to set tariffs no one else can audit. Vow-Breaker Wake wants tomorrow. Pale Saint Pact wants the freight surcharge to stop climbing. Nobody pretends anymore; the boundary lines get repainted in daylight. Legal filings over Ceibo's Breach IV Dome arrive faster than the courts can docket them. When Brothers of Choir and Pale Saint Pact finally close, it will be Carrion Wake standing between them, holding family on both sides of the picket line. The fuse is lit at both ends and burning politely.",
